This product builds on and includes third-party work:

- SAM 2 / SAM 2.1 (Meta Platforms, Inc.), Apache License 2.0
  https://github.com/facebookresearch/sam2
  Used as a library and as the teacher model. The released sam2-lite models contain SAM 2.1
  weights (memory encoder, mask decoder and a fine-tuned memory attention).

- src/sam2lite/eval/third_party/sav_benchmark.py: SAM 2's J&F evaluator, vendored unmodified,
  with its licenses in the same folder:
    BSD License, SAM 2 Eval software (Meta Platforms, Inc.)
    BSD 3-Clause License, DAVIS: Densely Annotated VIdeo Segmentation (davis2017-evaluation)
    MIT License, Rex Cheng (vos-benchmark)

- timm (PyTorch Image Models), Apache License 2.0
  https://github.com/huggingface/pytorch-image-models
  Provides the MobileNetV4 backbone and its ImageNet-pretrained weights.

The models were distilled on frames of the DAVIS 2017 dataset, which does not publish an
explicit data license. No DAVIS videos or frames are redistributed, and the models are released
for non-commercial research use.
